1
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:01,960
(Leonard:)Why?

2
00:00:02,124 --> 00:00:04,464
(Sheldon:)The learning opportunities
would be abundant.

3
00:00:04,627 --> 00:00:05,707
(Sheldon:)Additionally...

4
00:00:05,878 --> 00:00:08,468
(Sheldon:)...I like having my belly scratched.

5
00:00:10,716 --> 00:00:12,636
- Hey, Penny. How was work?
- Great.

6
00:00:12,802 --> 00:00:16,802
(Penny:)I hope I'm a waitress at
the Cheesecake Factory for my whole life.

7
00:00:16,972 --> 00:00:18,352
(Sheldon:)Was that sarcasm?

8
00:00:19,016 --> 00:00:20,146
(Sheldon:)No.

9
00:00:20,309 --> 00:00:21,519
(Sheldon:)Was that sarcasm?

10
00:00:21,977 --> 00:00:23,477
(Sheldon:)Yes.

11
00:00:23,646 --> 00:00:25,856
- Was that sarcasm?
- Stop it.

12
00:00:27,316 --> 00:00:28,646
Penny?

13
00:00:28,818 --> 00:00:31,068
(Sheldon:)- You appear to have a package here.
- Oh, thanks.

14
00:00:31,237 --> 00:00:32,817
It must be the beret I ordered.

15
00:00:32,988 --> 00:00:35,738
(Penny:)A couple of months ago.
It was back-ordered.

16
00:00:36,325 --> 00:00:38,245
(Sheldon:)Did you know the beret
is an example...

17
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:42,001
...of a piece of women's fashion
adapted from male military uniforms?

18
00:00:42,164 --> 00:00:46,004
(Sheldon:)Another fascinating example
is the epaulet.

19
00:00:47,378 --> 00:00:50,588
(Leonard:)He's not lying.
He does find that fascinating.

20
00:00:51,507 --> 00:00:52,677
Okay, look, whatever.

21
00:00:52,842 --> 00:00:55,842
(Penny:)It's not like I'm running up and down
the streets buying berets.

22
00:00:56,011 --> 00:00:59,261
I bought one a month ago
when it was back-ordered. It finally arrived.

